#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""doit mode for Jot, the self-hosted notes and todos.

  Type to capture: the first row adds what you typed, read the way Jot reads
  it ("Dentist tomorrow 10am #health", "Gym every mon and thu 7am", "Zahnarzt
  morgen um 10", "Shopping: milk, eggs, bread", a trailing " !" pins). The rows
  below are what it finds among your notes and todos.

  Empty, it's your day: overdue, today, the next week, then pinned notes and
  the rest. Enter completes a task (a repeating one moves to its next date)
  and opens a note in Jot; a checklist opens in place, Enter ticks a check,
  and typing adds one. Tab: snooze, tomorrow, reschedule (type a date the
  same way), pin, archive, trash, copy, open in Jot. #label shows a label.

Settings in ~/.config/doit/jot.toml:

  server = "https://jot.example.com"
  username = "me"          # optional; asked for at sign-in otherwise

As a launcher mode:

  [[provider]]
  name = "jot"
  exec = "~/.config/doit/providers/jot"
  prefix = "j "

or on its own: doit -m jot, or this script with --launch.

Everything is cached (mode 600) under ~/.cache/doit/jot, so it opens at
once and captures offline; changes go to the server as soon as it's there.
"""

